#: ../../source/explore/astartes.rst:4
msgid "Sampling with Astartes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/explore/astartes.rst:6
msgid ""
"**Chemotools** focuses on preprocessing and modeling spectral data, but "
"robust model validation starts with how you split your data. This is "
"where **Astartes** comes in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/explore/astartes.rst:8
msgid ""
"`Astartes <https://github.com/JacksonBurns/astartes>`_ is a Python "
"library for rigorous dataset splitting (sampling). It serves as a drop-in"
" replacement for ``sklearn.model_selection.train_test_split`` but offers "
"\"rational\" sampling algorithms like **Kennard-Stone** and **SPXY**, "
"which are essential in chemometrics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/explore/astartes.rst:11
msgid "Synergy with Chemotools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/explore/astartes.rst:13
msgid ""
"While ``chemotools`` provides the transformers to clean your spectra, "
"``astartes`` ensures your training set is statistically representative of"
" your domain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/explore/astartes.rst:15
msgid ""
"**Chemotools**: Preprocessing (Smoothing, Baseline correction, "
"Derivatives)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/explore/astartes.rst:16
msgid "**Astartes**: Calibration set selection (Kennard-Stone, SPXY)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/explore/astartes.rst:18
msgid ""
"Using them together allows you to build robust chemometric pipelines that"
" are validated on rigorously selected data."
msgstr ""

